# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# TikuGrab from the Applications menu: the whole desk grabbed without
# TikuGrab in it, then one window alone -- the desktop taking both, since
# an application cannot see the desk, and saying where each went.  Then a
# delayed grab, counting down in the Deskbar's tray, cancelled from there.
wait 20
click 980 40
wait 4
menu-pick Applications
wait 4
expect-menu TikuGrab
menu-pick TikuGrab
wait 30
expect-title TikuGrab
note the list offers the whole desk first, and it is chosen
expect-narrate Whole desk
key g ctrl
wait 40
expect-narrate Saved as tiku-desk-
shot /tmp/trk_grab_desk.png
note one window alone: the next row down, the desk's Tracker window
key Down
wait 4
key g ctrl
wait 40
expect-narrate Saved as tiku-window-
shot /tmp/trk_grab_window.png
note a delayed grab counts down beside the Deskbar's clock, as the
note application's own tray icon
click 118 10
wait 4
menu-pick 10 Seconds
wait 4
key g ctrl
wait 8
expect-narrate Grabbing in
shot /tmp/trk_grab_tray.png
note a click on that icon is the application's to hear: it cancels
click 880 154
wait 8
expect-narrate Capture cancelled.
shot /tmp/trk_grab_cancel.png
key w ctrl
wait 10
expect-no-title TikuGrab
